			<div class="content" id="post-content-4848233">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Comedy</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> An initial standard page going over the published editions of the book, and a log of incomplete and poorly copied extracts of the text without magic supposedly due to low quality. Followed by an up-to-date article documenting a edited copy of the tome, with a log of the different corrections made by a disenfranchised undergraduate of the establishment that require the book. Containment procedures allow for the book to be borrowed by approved request.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A secondhand university thaumaturgy textbook which is defunct and a scam, corrected by a angry ex-student (of the institution using it as required reading) to make it functional.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;whatever</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;whatever</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The book is drawn to the foundation's attention when it is incredulously found via web-crawlers on online book. It is quickly scrubbed from the website due to Foundation concerns about secrecy. A team of researchers are tasked with tracking down copies of the book but all that can be found are monochrome, poorly reproduced photocopies which are useless assisting thaumaturgical practices.</p>
<p>They receive a package from a disgruntled student of a only to discover it is a textbook for a specific professor who charges $25,000 USD (or relative small fortune) or &quot;a year's servitude to dark forces&quot; for it. The book is covered in angry notes expressing frustration in the inaccuracies of it such as &quot; What am I supposed to use?? Pig's blood or wolf?&quot; and &quot;There's no godsdamn way that is an acceptable salt circle&quot;, as well as several corrections in order to make the rituals and magic work as intended. The Foundation reclassifies the published versions as non-anomalous and classifies the only anomalous version to be the corrected one.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The thaumaturgy methods and descriptions in an academic way and the premise that not even magic prevents you from being screwed over by the educational system.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Would appreciate idea on how the actual corrected book is anomalous and not just containing data that can be used to create anomalies, and any areas of thaumaturgy on the SCP universe I should try and include in the photocopy example extracts?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

